"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued August 16 at 6:36PM MDT until August 16 at 9:30PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...South Central Weld County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 930 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 636 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area. Between 1.5 and 2 inches of rain\nhave fallen.\n\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nBox Elder Creek, Sanborn Draw, South Platte River, Crow Creek and\nLost Creek. Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1 inch are\nexpected over the area. This additional rain will result in minor\nflooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nKersey, Riverside Reservoir, Hardin and Masters.","ends":"2026-08-16T21:30:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Weld, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8cb7fcbb719c441287c4ec832c9b303e0f92090a.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8cb7fcbb719c441287c4ec832c9b303e0f92090a.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued August 16 at 5:38PM MDT until August 16 at 8:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Northern Morgan County in northeastern Colorado...\nNortheast Weld County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 800 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 538 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area. Up to 1 inch of rain has fallen.\n\n- Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are expected over the\narea. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nNew Raymer, Stoneham, Antelope Springs, Weldona, Jackson\nReservoir, Goodrich, Orchard and Buckingham.","ends":"2026-08-16T20:00:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Morgan, CO; Weld, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8039354aa1d754eb0c15e7a8a332ebdbba69f9ef.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8039354aa1d754eb0c15e7a8a332ebdbba69f9ef.001.1"},{"event":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch issued August 16 at 2:07PM MDT until August 16 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"THE NATIONAL WEATHER SERVICE HAS ISSUED SEVERE THUNDERSTORM WATCH\n587 IN EFFECT UNTIL 9 PM MDT THIS EVENING FOR THE FOLLOWING AREAS\n\nIN COLORADO THIS WATCH INCLUDES 12 COUNTIES\n\nIN EAST CENTRAL COLORADO\n\nELBERT                LINCOLN\n\nIN NORTHEAST COLORADO\n\nADAMS                 ARAPAHOE              DENVER\nDOUGLAS               LOGAN                 MORGAN\nPHILLIPS              SEDGWICK              WASHINGTON\nWELD\n\nTHIS INCLUDES THE CITIES OF AKRON, AURORA, CASTLE ROCK,\nCENTENNIAL, DENVER, DENVER INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT, ELIZABETH,\nFORT MORGAN, GREELEY, HOLYOKE, JULESBURG, KIOWA, LIMON, PARKER,\nSTERLING, THORNTON, WESTMINSTER, AND WINDSOR.","ends":"2026-08-16T21:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Adams, CO; Arapahoe, CO; Denver, CO; Douglas, CO; Elbert, CO; Lincoln, CO; Logan, CO; Morgan, CO; Phillips, CO; Sedgwick, CO; Washington, CO; Weld, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b1e6f8e2ba2bd466551a7c90038f7d5dc203b905.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b1e6f8e2ba2bd466551a7c90038f7d5dc203b905.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-16T23:59:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 162359 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 559 PM MDT Sun Aug 16 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Scattered thunderstorms possible through this evening. A few of them could become strong to sever